      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ARABELLA STAR (1) was out of the money when resuming from a spell last start over 1000m at Sandown-Hillside, beaten 3.5 lengths. Finds the right race this time and can get the job done. DIHHERI (5) is a handy type who resumes after a break of six months, which followed a poor run at Pakenham that was too bad to be true. Fitter for a recent trial win and has to be included.  DIRTY DIANA (9) has been in the money at her last couple of runs, the latest when third over 1000m at Moe. Rises in grade here, but racing more consistently than most and can feature. TIPSY GYPSY (7) returns and has been fitted with a sound Flemington jumpout. Still relatively lightly raced and can make her presence felt fresh.",
